    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1283">

                <pb facs="0881" n="765" xml:id="pg765"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/21.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Vice Consul Simpich.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-11-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 22, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mexican Petroleum Company and Huasteca Petroleum Company, Casiano, seventy miles
                    south of Tampico, report that General Aguilar has demanded $100,000 from
                    them.</p>
                <p>Bring to attention of Carranza and informally request him to issue orders to
                    Aguilar to withdraw this demand and cease molesting these American
                    companies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
